//! check: fail(E0817)
//! phase: typecheck
// Exercise 20-5: a broken promise. `build` allocates; the attribute says
// it does not. PENDING: perf-contract verification (I15, wolf-lang#180).
// Until a checker exists the attribute is refused by name — E0817, "not
// implemented yet" — so the compiler never runs the lie. The verifying
// compiler will reject this program for its CONTENT instead, with a code
// today's catalog does not assign. lupin reads no attribute
// (wolf-interp#174) and still prints 3.
#[noalloc]
fn build() -> List[int] {
    var xs = List[int]()
    (mut xs).push(1)
    (mut xs).push(2)
    (mut xs).push(3)
    xs
}
fn main() -> !int {
    let xs = build()
    print("{xs.len}")
    0
}
